{"parentUuid":"721ccd6c-9a1a-4c73-b877-b864881ca699","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NL6JsgAY7QzVZsLTPv3Yob","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaProof successor 2026 IMO formal mathematics Google DeepMind\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AI achieves silver-medal standard solving International Mathematical Olympiad problems — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/ai-solves-imo-problems-at-silver-medal-level/\"},{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced version of Gemini with Deep Think officially achieves gold-medal standard at the International Mathematical Olympiad — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/advanced-version-of-gemini-with-deep-think-officially-achieves-gold-medal-standard-at-the-international-mathematical-olympiad/\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind's Latest Paper in Nature Unveils Most Powerful Mathematical Model for IMO\",\"url\":\"https://eu.36kr.com/en/p/3551304246589575\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind on X: \\\"We’re presenting the first AI to solve International Mathematical Olympiad problems at a silver medalist level.🥈 It combines AlphaProof, a new breakthrough model for formal reasoning, and AlphaGeometry 2, an improved version of our previous system. 🧵 https://t.co/U0OFXBia8n https://t.co/h2mcLLRJjk\\\" / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/1816498082860667086?lang=en\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind and Google.org announce AI for Math Initiative\",\"url\":\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/ai-for-math/\"},{\"title\":\"[Research Press Release] Artificial intelligence: A mathematics medal-worthy AI system (Nature) | Nature Portfolio\",\"url\":\"https://www.natureasia.com/en/info/press-releases/detail/9147\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof and AlphaGeometry 2 Solve IMO Math Problems · innFactory AI Consulting - AI Strategy & Consulting\",\"url\":\"https://innfactory.ai/en/blog/breakthrough-in-mathematical-problem-solving-alphaproof-and-alphageometry-2-from-google-deepmind/\"},{\"title\":\"AI math genius delivers 100% accurate results\",\"url\":\"https://phys.org/news/2025-11-ai-math-genius-accurate-results.html\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind claims its AI performs better than International Mathematical Olympiad gold medalists | TechCrunch\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/07/deepmind-claims-its-ai-performs-better-than-international-mathematical-olympiad-gold-medalists/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding AlphaProof's successor in 2026:\n\n## AlphaProof and Its 2026 Successor\n\nAlphaProof is a reinforcement-learning based system for formal math reasoning that, together with AlphaGeometry 2, solved four out of six problems from the 2024 International Mathematical Olympiad (IMO), achieving the same level as a silver medalist.\n\nHowever, the successor system has now arrived. An advanced version of Gemini Deep Think solved five out of the six IMO problems, earning 35 total points and achieving gold-medal level performance at the 2025 IMO.\n\n### Key Differences from AlphaProof:\n\nUnlike the 2024 AlphaProof and AlphaGeometry systems that required experts to first translate problems from natural language into domain-specific languages like Lean, the 2025 Gemini model operated end-to-end in natural language, producing rigorous mathematical proofs directly from official problem descriptions within the 4.5-hour competition time limit.\n\nThe advanced Gemini Deep Think incorporates latest research techniques including parallel thinking, and was trained on novel reinforcement learning techniques that can leverage multi-step reasoning, problem-solving and theorem-proving data.\n\nThis represents a significant advancement, moving from formal proof-based systems to end-to-end natural language reasoning while achieving even higher performance on IMO problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ddeed8e7-f00b-4e7e-b9b8-aca9b23ecbfe","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:25.199Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"721ccd6c-9a1a-4c73-b877-b864881ca699","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6e2efc05-2cd8-48ea-bc3c-7964758b5959","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MmmoUEQ3bMcatarK4fWw4D","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepSeek-Prover-V2 Goedel-Prover Lean theorem proving benchmark 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Prover-V2 · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Prover-V2\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-Prover-V2: Open-Source AI for Lean 4 Formal Theorem Proving | by My Social | 𝐀𝐈 𝐦𝐨𝐧𝐤𝐬.𝐢𝐨 | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/aimonks/deepseek-prover-v2-open-source-ai-for-lean-4-formal-theorem-proving-ab7f9910576b\"},{\"title\":\"[2504.21801] DeepSeek-Prover-V2: Advancing Formal Mathematical Reasoning via Reinforcement Learning for Subgoal Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.21801\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek Launches Prover-V2 Open-Source LLM for Formal Math Proofs - InfoQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/05/deepseek-prover-v2-formal-proof/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-Prover-V2: Neural Prover in Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/deepseek-prover-v2\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-Prover-V2: Advancing Formal Mathematical Reasoning via Reinforcement Learning for Subgoal Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.21801v1\"},{\"title\":\"Goedel-Prover-V2: Scaling Formal Theorem Proving with ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.03613\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-Prover: Advancing Theorem Proving in LLMs ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.14333\"},{\"title\":\"Goedel-Prover\",\"url\":\"https://goedel-lm.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepSeek-Prover-V2: Advancing Formal Mathematical ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.21801\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about DeepSeek-Prover-V2, Goedel-Prover, and their performance on Lean theorem proving benchmarks:\n\n## DeepSeek-Prover-V2\n\nDeepSeek-Prover-V2 is an open-source large language model designed for formal theorem proving in Lean 4, with initialization data collected through a recursive theorem proving pipeline powered by DeepSeek-V3. The model is released in two model sizes: a 7B parameter version built upon DeepSeek-Prover-V1.5-Base with an extended context length of up to 32K tokens, and a 671B parameter version trained on DeepSeek-V3-Base.\n\n### Performance on Benchmarks\n\nThe resulting model, DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B, achieves state-of-the-art performance in neural theorem proving, reaching 88.9% pass ratio on the MiniF2F-test and solving 49 out of 658 problems from PutnamBench. DeepSeek-Prover-V2 introduces ProverBench, a benchmark dataset comprising 325 problems, with 15 formalized from AIME competitions (AIME 24 and 25) and the remaining 310 problems drawn from curated textbook examples and educational tutorials.\n\n## Goedel-Prover Comparison\n\nDeepSeek-Prover-V2–671B achieves 82.4% pass@32 on miniF2F, while Goedel-Prover-V2–8B (∼80× smaller) attains 84.6%, and the Goedel-Prover-V2–32B surpasses it with 88.1% (up to 90.4% with self-correction). Goedel-Prover-V2's 32B model achieves pass@32 accuracy of 88.1% on MiniF2F, with 90.4% after 2 rounds of error-correction, exceeding the previous state-of-the-art DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B's 82.4% while using far fewer parameters.\n\nThe search results demonstrate that while DeepSeek-Prover-V2 set initial benchmarks in 2025, Goedel-Prover-V2 subsequently achieved superior performance on key metrics with much smaller model sizes through verifier-guided error correction techniques.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5acf1546-14dd-46d0-83a0-c982d39af26a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:26.649Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e2efc05-2cd8-48ea-bc3c-7964758b5959","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2e6880e0-86ca-4e9e-a4c7-4be88e879e14","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RppTHrjMfs4q7JTytHbX2v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"autoformalization Lean Coq natural language 2026 LLM benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Autoformalization in the Era of Large Language Models: A Survey\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.23486v1\"},{\"title\":\"Theorem Proving and Machine Learning in the age of LLMs: SoA and Future Perspectives - EuroProofNet\",\"url\":\"https://europroofnet.github.io/wg5-edinburgh25/\"},{\"title\":\"Work in progress PROCESS-DRIVEN AUTOFORMALIZATION IN LEAN 4\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.01940\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - zhaoyu-li/DL4TP: [COLM 2024] A Survey on Deep Learning for Theorem Proving · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zhaoyu-li/DL4TP\"},{\"title\":\"Autoformalization in the Era of Large Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.23486\"},{\"title\":\"Reliable Evaluation and Benchmarks for Statement ...\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.907.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Translating Natural Language into Lean 4 through Multi- ...\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1586v2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Process-Driven Autoformalization in Lean 4 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=k8KsI84Ds7\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematics in the Age of Large Language Models | by Przemek Chojecki | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://pchojecki.medium.com/mathematics-in-the-age-of-large-language-models-40674573acfa\"},{\"title\":\"FM@atlascomputing.org Note: please email with additional comments or questions\",\"url\":\"https://atlascomputing.org/ai-assisted-fv-toolchain.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding autoformalization, Lean, Coq, natural language, and LLM benchmarks in 2026:\n\n## Recent Developments in Autoformalization\n\nAutoformalization is a research direction focused on automating the translation from informal mathematics to formal language. Syntactic accuracy refers to the ability to correctly translate into formal language, that is, whether the final formal result can pass the type check of Lean, Coq and other environments.\n\n## Recent Benchmarks and Datasets (2024-2025)\n\nSeveral key benchmarks have emerged recently:\n\n- FormalAlign: Automated Alignment Evaluation for Autoformalization (ICLR 2025) and Herald: A Natural Language Annotated Lean 4 Dataset (ICLR 2025) represent the latest evaluation frameworks.\n\n- The FormL4 benchmark was introduced to evaluate autoformalization in Lean 4, designed to comprehensively evaluate the autoformalization capabilities of large language models (LLMs), encompassing both statements and proofs in natural and formal languages.\n\n- ProofNet pairs hundreds of undergraduate-level theorems and proofs with Lean formalizations.\n\n## LLM-Based Approaches\n\nApplications include designing co-pilot systems for theorem provers like Coq, Lean, or Isabelle, auto-formalising mathematical concepts and proofs from textbooks or research papers, and human-machine collaboration workflows in proof construction.\n\nJiang et al. (2024) translated two of the largest corpora: Archive of Formal Proofs (Isabelle) and mathlib4 (Lean4) into natural language using GPT-4.\n\nThese developments show active progress in 2024-2025 toward building better benchmarks and improving LLM capabilities for autoformalization in Lean and other proof assistants.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8245835f-4adb-4df6-8b85-b432ebc8c4b4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:27.713Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e6880e0-86ca-4e9e-a4c7-4be88e879e14","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"532cbd0f-9519-41d5-a7d0-64f25f9c1974","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BsfeA5CNnH8EECL1b3aKkz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gemini Deep Think 2.5 mathematics optimization reasoning\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Gemini Deep Think: Redefining the Future of Scientific Research — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/accelerating-mathematical-and-scientific-discovery-with-gemini-deep-think/\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluating Gemini 2.5 Deep Think's math capabilities | Epoch AI\",\"url\":\"https://epoch.ai/blog/deep-think-math\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini 2.5 Deep Think Parallelizes Creative Problem-Solving - InfoQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/08/gemini-2-5-deep-think/\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini 2.5: Deep Think is now rolling out\",\"url\":\"https://blog.google/products/gemini/gemini-2-5-deep-think/\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini 2.5 Deep Think explained: Everything you need to know\",\"url\":\"https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/feature/Gemini-25-Deep-Think-explained\"},{\"title\":\"Solving years-old math problems with Gemini 2.5 Deep Think - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QoXRfTb7ves\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini 2.5 Deep Think: Google’s Revolutionary Parallel Thinking AI Explained – LaoZhang-AI\",\"url\":\"https://blog.laozhang.ai/ai-models/gemini-2-5-deep-think-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"Google Gemini 2.5 Deep Think Launch! IMO Gold Medal Endorsed, Can the New AI Champion Reshape the Future?\",\"url\":\"https://news.aibase.com/news/20197\"},{\"title\":\"Google Gemini 2.5 Deep Think : The best ever AI is here | by Mehul Gupta | Data Science in Your Pocket | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/data-science-in-your-pocket/google-gemini-2-5-deep-think-the-best-ever-ai-is-here-cdffa542de7e\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini 3.0 Pro vs. 2.5 Pro: Reasoning (ARC-AGI-2), Coding & Math Benchmarks Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://vertu.com/lifestyle/gemini-3-0-vs-gemini-2-5-pro-google-sets-new-performance-standards-in-2025/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Gemini 2.5 Deep Think, particularly regarding mathematics optimization and reasoning:\n\n## Overview\n\nGemini 2.5 Deep Think is specifically optimized as a reasoning model, meaning it can \"think\" longer than a regular model to figure out, consider or reason over a prompt, before coming to a conclusion and generating an output.\n\n## Key Reasoning Architecture\n\nThe model's core innovation lies in its parallel-thinking approach, with which the model can explore multiple ideas simultaneously, revising and combining them before answering. The model uses novel reinforcement learning techniques during training, which encourage the model to make use of these extended reasoning paths to test multiple hypotheses at once.\n\n## Mathematical Performance\n\nThe model achieved exceptional results in mathematics. In the summer of 2025, an advanced version of Gemini Deep Think achieved Gold-medal standard at the International Mathematics Olympiad (IMO) and these results demonstrated the model could reason through some of the most challenging math and programming problems designed for students.\n\nAn advanced version of Gemini Deep Think helped resolve long-standing bottlenecks across algorithms, ML and combinatorial optimization, information theory, and economics. Specifically, Gemini broke deadlocks on classic computer science problems like \"Max-Cut\" (efficiently splitting networks) and the \"Steiner Tree\" (connecting high-dimensional points) by thinking outside the box.\n\n## Optimization Capabilities\n\nDeep Think particularly excels at tough coding problems in which problem formulation and careful consideration of tradeoffs and time complexity is paramount. Gemini 2.5 Deep Think achieves state-of-the-art performance across LiveCodeBench V6, which measures competitive code performance, and Humanity's Last Exam, a challenging benchmark that measures expertise in different domains, including science and math.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4eb706d1-0b6c-4030-9a84-9ccf74bbb10a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:28.689Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"532cbd0f-9519-41d5-a7d0-64f25f9c1974","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
