{"parentUuid":"c5bd9a1b-dbc9-4780-9b17-1bd27aff27aa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NszJMVdG3uZH9DyBujtKbU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Lean Copilot LeanInteract LeanDojo 2026 development tools\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - lean-dojo/LeanCopilot: LLMs as Copilots for Theorem Proving in Lean · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lean-dojo/LeanCopilot\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Copilot: Large Language Models as Copilots for Theorem Proving in Lean\",\"url\":\"https://leandojo.org/leancopilot.html\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Copilot download | SourceForge.net\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/projects/lean-copilot.mirror/\"},{\"title\":\"AI-Driven Formal Theorem Proving in the Lean Ecosystem\",\"url\":\"https://leandojo.org/\"},{\"title\":\"LeanCopilot/README.md at main · lean-dojo/LeanCopilot\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lean-dojo/LeanCopilot/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"LeanCopilot/LeanCopilot.lean at main · lean-dojo/LeanCopilot\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lean-dojo/LeanCopilot/blob/main/LeanCopilot.lean\"},{\"title\":\"lean‑dojo/LeanCopilot - Reservoir\",\"url\":\"https://reservoir.lean-lang.org/@lean-dojo/LeanCopilot\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Copilot: Large Language Models as Copilots for Theorem Proving in Lean\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2404.12534v2\"},{\"title\":\"LeanCopilot/README.md at main · jamsyd/LeanCopilot\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jamsyd/LeanCopilot/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Anima Anandkumar on LinkedIn: GitHub - lean-dojo/LeanCopilot: LLMs as Copilots for Theorem Proving in… | 37 comments\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/anima-anandkumar_github-lean-dojoleancopilot-llms-as-copilots-activity-7139963032452923394-_T0r\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Lean Copilot, LeanInteract, and LeanDojo as development tools in 2026:\n\n## Lean Copilot\n\nLean Copilot allows large language models (LLMs) to be used natively in Lean for proof automation, e.g., suggesting tactics/premises and searching for proofs. You can use built-in models from LeanDojo or bring your own models that run either locally (with or without GPUs) or on the cloud.\n\n### Key Features:\n- The tactic suggest_tactics generates tactic suggestions, and search_proof combines LLM-generated tactics with aesop to search for multi-tactic proofs.\n- The select_premises tactic retrieves a list of potentially useful premises, currently using the retriever in LeanDojo to select premises from a fixed snapshot of Lean and mathlib4.\n\n## LeanDojo\n\nRecent developments include LeanDojo-v2: A Comprehensive Library for AI-Assisted Theorem Proving in Lean from a 2025 NeurIPS workshop. The platform provides the foundation for models used by Lean Copilot and hosts datasets for AI-assisted theorem proving research.\n\n## Technical Details\n\nLean Copilot is supported on Linux, macOS, Windows and Windows WSL platforms. Lean Copilot supports two kinds of models: generators and encoders.\n\n**Note:** The search results do not contain specific information about \"LeanInteract\" as a distinct development tool.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"16ea567a-1f72-4713-821e-5a258936140b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:38.737Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c5bd9a1b-dbc9-4780-9b17-1bd27aff27aa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dbaa10d9-ce7c-44c5-8d61-7dc359a49ed4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VW3haas9VNntEpkBEyUZZ8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AI agent formal verification optimization solver proof certificate 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"RocqSmith: Can Automatic Optimization Forge Better Proof Agents?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.05762\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Reasoning Meets LLMs: Toward AI for Mathematics and Verification – Communications of the ACM\",\"url\":\"https://cacm.acm.org/research/formal-reasoning-meets-llms-toward-ai-for-mathematics-and-verification/\"},{\"title\":\"Prediction: AI will make formal verification go mainstream — Martin Kleppmann’s blog\",\"url\":\"https://martin.kleppmann.com/2025/12/08/ai-formal-verification.html\"},{\"title\":\"AgentGuard: Runtime Verification of AI Agents\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.23864v1\"},{\"title\":\"Meta Researchers Show AI Agents Can Verify Code Without Running It — and Hit 93% Accuracy - DevOps.com\",\"url\":\"https://devops.com/meta-researchers-show-ai-agents-can-verify-code-without-running-it-and-hit-93-accuracy/\"},{\"title\":\"The ClawHavoc Campaign: How Malicious AI Agent Skills Exposed the Verification Gap — clawbot.blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.clawbot.blog/blog/the-clawhavoc-campaign-how-malicious-ai-agent-skills-exposed-the-verification-ga/\"},{\"title\":\"Leanstral: Mistral AI's Open-Source Agent for Formal Proofs | AIToolly\",\"url\":\"https://aitoolly.com/ai-news/article/2026-03-17-leanstral-mistral-ais-open-source-agent-for-trustworthy-coding-and-formal-proof-engineering\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Verification in the Age of AI - Toby's Blog - verse.systems\",\"url\":\"https://verse.systems/blog/post/2026-03-05-formal-verification-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"AI and Humans Verify Fields Medal Proof for the First Time\",\"url\":\"https://spectrum.ieee.org/ai-proof-verification\"},{\"title\":\"2026 Tutorials & Workshops | DVCON 2026\",\"url\":\"https://dvcon.org/program/2026/2026-tutorials-workshops\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for \"AI agent formal verification optimization solver proof certificate 2026\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent Developments in AI Agent Formal Verification (2026)\n\n**Agentic Systems for Interactive Theorem Proving:**\nRecent work focuses on autonomous agentic systems for interactive theorem proving, which are a natural fit for this setting as their interaction loop closely resembles that of a human programmer. Research studies the applicability of automatic AI agent optimization methods to real-world agents in formal verification settings, focusing on automated theorem proving and assessing whether parts of fine-grained tuning of agentic systems, such as prompt design and control strategies, can be automated.\n\n**Proof Certificates and Verification:**\nFormal verification approaches output a binary pass/fail with a machine-readable proof certificate. Some implementations build formal models of permitted operations using SMT (Satisfiability Modulo Theories) solvers and analyze implementations to prove they cannot access APIs or endpoints outside declared sets.\n\n**Notable Tools and Systems:**\nMistral AI introduced Leanstral, the first open-source code agent specifically designed for the Lean 4 proof assistant, addressing the critical scaling bottleneck of human review in high-stakes AI code generation. AgentGuard is a framework for runtime verification of Agentic AI systems.\n\n**Recent Achievements:**\nFields Medal–winning mathematical work about optimal sphere packing in many dimensions is now formally verified by a human-AI collaboration, signaling rapid progress in AI's abilities to assist with mathematics.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"20ed11b4-4ab1-4bc0-86d9-b0bf410d9460","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:40.096Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbaa10d9-ce7c-44c5-8d61-7dc359a49ed4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"edfbb315-6034-4433-a355-e5bc8f77e49d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TuUHGoNQC8rDZYM3pRv2RW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"PutnamBench\" OR \"miniF2F\" 2026 state of the art LLM theorem prover\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MiniF2F-Dafny: LLM-Guided Mathematical Theorem Proving via Auto-Active Verification (Dafny 2026) - POPL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://popl26.sigplan.org/details/dafny-2026-papers/16/MiniF2F-Dafny-LLM-Guided-Mathematical-Theorem-Proving-via-Auto-Active-Verification\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2026\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.22819\"},{\"title\":\"miniF2F-Dafny: LLM-Guided Mathematical Theorem Proving via Auto-Active Verification\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.10187\"},{\"title\":\"PUTNAMBENCH: Evaluating Neural Theorem-Provers on ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2407.11214\"},{\"title\":\"STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=zWArMedNuW\"},{\"title\":\"Discover and Prove: An Open-source Agentic Framework for Hard Mode Automated Theorem Proving in Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.15839\"},{\"title\":\"Technical Report GOEDEL-PROVER-V2: SCALING FORMAL THEOREM\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.03613\"},{\"title\":\"PUTNAMBENCH: A Multilingual Competition-Mathematics Benchmark for\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=vqW1VRFeVP\"},{\"title\":\"MINIF2F-DAFNY: LLM-Guided Mathematical Theorem ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.10187\"},{\"title\":\"MiniF2F | alphaXiv\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/benchmarks/university-of-pittsburgh/minif2f\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about PutnamBench and miniF2F in the context of 2026 state-of-the-art LLM theorem provers:\n\n## PutnamBench\n\nPutnamBench focuses on college-level mathematics competition problems sourced from the William Lowell Putnam Mathematical Competition years 1962-2023, comprising 644 problems covering algebra, analysis, number theory, geometry, combinatorics, probability, and set theory.\n\n### Recent State-of-the-Art Results:\n\nHILBERT achieved 99.2% on miniF2F in Lean and 70.0% on PutnamBench. Goedel-Prover-V2-32B under pass@184 and error correction solves 86 on PutnamBench, securing the best open-source theorem prover on the leaderboard.\n\nThe system Discover and Prove (DAP) is the first system to formally prove 36 theorems in PutnamBench Hard Mode.\n\n## miniF2F\n\nThe MiniF2F dataset is a 488 problem dataset comprising high-school mathematics competition problems, with some particularly challenging problems sourced from the AMC, AIME and IMO competitions.\n\n### Recent State-of-the-Art Results:\n\nHILBERT reaches 99.2% pass rate on miniF2F. Goedel-Prover-V2-32B achieves 90.4% after 2 rounds of error-correction on MiniF2F, exceeding the previous state-of-the-art DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B's 82.4% while using far fewer parameters.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9d401af6-5eb0-4508-9264-41b1dfcb606f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:40.617Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"edfbb315-6034-4433-a355-e5bc8f77e49d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1846d12c-c243-4bfb-994f-e629fdec48c2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WM1PFz7j4iVFVbhPSyMw3M","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Kimina-Prover Numina Llemma Lean 4 reasoning 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AI-MO/Kimina-Prover-72B · Hugging Face\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/AI-MO/Kimina-Prover-72B\"},{\"title\":\"Kimina-Prover Preview: Towards Large Formal Reasoning Models with Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.11354v1\"},{\"title\":\"kimina-prover-rl/recipe/kimina_prover_rl/README.md at main · project-numina/kimina-prover-rl\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/project-numina/kimina-prover-rl/blob/main/recipe/kimina_prover_rl/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"[Literature Review] Kimina-Prover Preview: Towards Large Formal Reasoning Models with Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/en/review/kimina-prover-preview-towards-large-formal-reasoning-models-with-reinforcement-learning\"},{\"title\":\"Kimina-Prover-RL\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/AI-MO/kimina-prover-rl\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - MoonshotAI/Kimina-Prover-Preview: Technical report of Kimina-Prover Preview. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MoonshotAI/Kimina-Prover-Preview\"},{\"title\":\"project-numina · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/project-numina\"},{\"title\":\"Publications - Marco Dos Santos\",\"url\":\"https://marco-dossantos.github.io/publications/\"},{\"title\":\"[2504.11354] Kimina-Prover Preview: Towards Large Formal Reasoning Models with Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11354\"},{\"title\":\"kimina prover\",\"url\":\"https://app.icerm.brown.edu/assets/553/8887/8887_5083_042520251130_Slides.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Kimina-Prover, Numina, and Lean 4 reasoning:\n\n## Kimina-Prover Overview\n\nKimina-Prover-72B is a theorem proving model developed by Project Numina and Kimi teams, focusing on competition style problem solving capabilities in Lean 4. Kimina-Prover is a large reasoning model for Lean 4 theorem proving developed through a training recipe combining autoformalization, SFT, and RL with a specific formal reasoning pattern.\n\n## Key Features and Performance\n\nKimina-Prover Preview pioneers a novel reasoning-driven exploration paradigm for formal theorem proving. Trained with a large-scale reinforcement learning pipeline from Qwen2.5-72B, Kimina-Prover demonstrates strong performance in Lean 4 proof generation by employing a structured reasoning pattern termed \"formal reasoning pattern,\" allowing the model to emulate human problem-solving strategies in Lean.\n\nKimina-Prover sets a new state-of-the-art on the miniF2F benchmark, reaching 80.7% with pass@8192. It was the first large reasoning model applied to theorem proving, and pushed the state-of-the-art on miniF2F (from 71% to 81% for the Preview version, and from 89% to 92% for the final version) and PutnamBench.\n\n## Open-Source Releases\n\nKimina-Prover-RL is an open-source training pipeline for formal theorem proving in Lean 4, based on a structured reasoning-then-generation paradigm inspired by DeepSeek-R1. This pipeline is a simplified version of the system used to train Kimina Prover, retaining its core components and offering full compatibility with the open-source Verl framework.\n\nNumina and Kimi have developed an open-source server called kimina-lean-server, which supports parallel proof checking at scale using Lean 4.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"574e0035-d91f-4181-b3ae-8677680a5731","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:42.480Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1846d12c-c243-4bfb-994f-e629fdec48c2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7