{"parentUuid":"20c06c0d-62ab-4efc-b7ad-0a8f9d1fd292","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FDGKBWoJQWGCwGUFF4dwR1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LddogTfuPELnHLR5z3RC99","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"AlphaEvolve successor formal verification optimization rectangle packing 2026"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2944,"cache_read_input_tokens":32689,"output_tokens":164,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2944},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3152,"output_tokens":164,"cache_read_input_tokens":32689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2944,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoxs3cWQUEd1PxiBFv9s","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"05ce9c23-5482-46be-be66-674750c2535c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:02.675Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"05ce9c23-5482-46be-be66-674750c2535c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"88dcafdf-a08f-4678-84c0-930bce6a1767","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LddogTfuPELnHLR5z3RC99","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaEvolve successor formal verification optimization rectangle packing 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"What GenAI Taught Us About the Future of Global Optimization | ORMS Today\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/do/10.1287/orms.2026.01.01/full/\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: An open source evolutionary coding agent for algorithm discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v1\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: LLM-Driven Code Evolution\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/alphaevolve-framework\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: an open-source evolutionary framework for algorithmic discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v4\"},{\"title\":\"ImprovEvolve: Ask AlphaEvolve to Improve the Input Solution and Then Improvise\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.10233v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2506.13131] AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131\"},{\"title\":\"Self-Evolving Agents | Yue Shui Blog\",\"url\":\"https://syhya.github.io/posts/2026-02-20-self-evolving-agents/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/392736011_AlphaEvolve_A_coding_agent_for_scientific_and_algorithmic_discovery\"},{\"title\":\"Magellan: Autonomous Discovery of Novel Compiler Optimization Heuristics with AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2601.21096v1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant developments related to AlphaEvolve successors and related work in 2026 involving formal verification, optimization, and rectangle packing:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n### Successors and Extensions to AlphaEvolve:\n\n1. **CodeEvolve**: An open-source evolutionary coding agent that not only matches AlphaEvolve's performance but surpasses it on five of six benchmarks. For rectangle packing (P4), CodeEvolve achieved an objective value identical to AlphaEvolve's up to the sixth decimal place, with a minor improvement on the seventh.\n\n2. **ImprovEvolve**: Evaluated on challenging problems from the AlphaEvolve paper, achieving new state-of-the-art results for hexagon packing in 11, 12, 15, and 16 hexagons.\n\n3. **Magellan**: An end-to-end compiler optimization agent powered by AlphaEvolve that evolves compiler passes by synthesizing and evaluating executable C++ heuristics.\n\n### Formal Verification Integration:\n\nAletheia is an agent for mathematical research with a core iterative Generate-Verify-Revise closed-loop mechanism, continuously optimizing solution paths and conclusion reliability through cyclic reasoning and formal verification.\n\n### Traditional Optimization Approach:\n\nA traditional optimization solver was not only able to match the solutions found by the AlphaEvolve team but also found even better solutions in some cases, particularly for rectangle packing problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"931db642-0acf-4094-a6d8-66f27ddd45c4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:09.518Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"05ce9c23-5482-46be-be66-674750c2535c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"20c06c0d-62ab-4efc-b7ad-0a8f9d1fd292","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"88dcafdf-a08f-4678-84c0-930bce6a1767","agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012CQ3pSXAdNHBrG1oNmNr3U","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"SeedProver\" OR \"STP\" self-play theorem prover 2026 benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=zWArMedNuW\"},{\"title\":\"STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2502.00212\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - kfdong/STP: The official implementation of \\\"Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving\\\"\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kfdong/STP\"},{\"title\":\"STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving | alphaXiv\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2502.00212\"},{\"title\":\"[2502.00212] STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.00212\"},{\"title\":\"Seed-Prover: Deep and Broad Reasoning for Automated Theorem Proving\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2507.23726v1\"},{\"title\":\"STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2502.00212\"},{\"title\":\"Beyond Limited Data: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2502.00212v1\"},{\"title\":\"Self-play Theorem Prover (STP) Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/self-play-theorem-prover-stp\"},{\"title\":\"STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers with Iterative Conjecturing and Proving\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=zWArMedNuW\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about both STP and Seed-Prover. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## STP (Self-play Theorem Prover)\n\nSTP is a Self-play Theorem Prover that simultaneously takes on two roles: a conjecturer, which proposes new conjectures that are challenging yet approachable, and a prover, which tries to prove them.\n\n### Key Benchmark Results\n\nWith 51.3 billion tokens generated during training in Lean, STP proves 28.5% of the statements in the LeanWorkbook dataset, doubling the previous best result of 13.1% achieved through expert iteration. The final model achieves state-of-the-art performance among whole-proof generation methods on miniF2F-test (65.0%), ProofNet-test (23.9%) and PutnamBench (8/644) with pass@3200.\n\n### Approach\n\nThe system draws inspiration from mathematicians who continuously develop new results by proposing novel conjectures or exercises and attempting to solve them. The conjecturer is trained iteratively on previously generated conjectures that are barely provable by the current prover, which incentivizes it to generate increasingly challenging conjectures over time.\n\n## Seed-Prover\n\nThere is also a separate system called Seed-Prover, a whole-proof model specialized in formal reasoning in Lean 4. Its most significant distinction from prior work lies in its adoption of lemma-style proving as the proof paradigm, which places lemmas at the center of the reasoning process.\n\nBoth systems represent recent advances in automated theorem proving using large language models, with STP being the primary system matching your search query and achieving state-of-the-art results in 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"06ae31b2-e6bc-4fe1-89d2-5cf84e046f4b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:10.000Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20c06c0d-62ab-4efc-b7ad-0a8f9d1fd292","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"06ae31b2-e6bc-4fe1-89d2-5cf84e046f4b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a73c288aed7cd9b98","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Re31AguoNCMU2nK687sAm9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我已经收集到足够信息。现在总结关键发现。\n\n# 2026 上半年 AI 形式化数学进展调研\n\n## 7 个最新工作概述（带具体数字）\n\n### 1. Goedel-Prover-V2（2025-08，arXiv 2508.03613）\n32B 模型在 miniF2F 上达到 pass@32 = 88.1%，2 轮 self-correction 后 90.4%；PutnamBench 上 pass@184 + 错误纠正解出 86/644。**关键意义**：用 80 倍更小的模型超越 DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B（82.4%）。开源社区追上闭源水位。\n\n### 2. HILBERT（Apple，ICLR 2026，arXiv 2509.22819）\nagentic 框架：informal LLM + 专用 prover LLM + Lean verifier + 语义检索器。miniF2F **99.2%**（比之前最好高 6.6 分），PutnamBench **70.0%**（462/660），把 SeedProver（50.4%）拉开近 20 分。核心思路是\"非形式推理 + 子目标递归分解 + 形式验证\"闭环。\n\n### 3. Kimina-Prover-72B（Numina/Moonshot）\nminiF2F 从 81% → **92%**（最终版），首个把 RL + reasoning pattern 真正用在形式证明上的大模型。配套放出 `kimina-lean-server` 支持大规模并行 Lean 4 校验。\n\n### 4. Leanstral（Mistral，2026-03-16）\n**首个真正面向工程仓库的 Lean 4 agent**。120B MoE / 6B 激活。bench 不是孤立题目，而是 FLT 项目里完整的 PR。pass@2 = 26.3 分（比 Sonnet 高 2.6），运行成本 **$36 vs Sonnet $549**——15 倍成本优势。Apache 2.0 开源，原生支持 lean-lsp-mcp。\n\n### 5. Gemini Deep Think（IMO 2025 金牌版，Nature 2026）\n**端到端自然语言**做 IMO，不需要先翻译成 Lean，5/6 题，35 分金牌。后续 Deep Think 在科研里破解 Max-Cut、Steiner Tree 这类经典 CS 难题——但**没有形式证明保证**，只是数值/启发式新解。\n\n### 6. STP（ICLR 2025，arXiv 2502.00212）\nself-play conjecturer + prover 架构，LeanWorkbook 上 28.5%（之前最好 13.1% 翻倍）。是 Goedel/Kimina 的训练数据来源之一。\n\n### 7. AlphaEvolve 后续（CodeEvolve、ImprovEvolve、Magellan）\n**与我们最直接相关**。CodeEvolve 在 6 个 bench 中 5 个超过 AlphaEvolve，包括矩形装箱（P4），目标值在第 7 位小数处比 AlphaEvolve 还好。ORMS 2026 一篇文章指出：\"**传统优化求解器不仅匹敌 AlphaEvolve，在矩形装箱上还能找到更好的解**\"——印证我们用 CP-SAT 走到底是对的。\n\n### 8. Autoformalization 工具链\nHerald（ICLR 2025）、FormalAlign（ICLR 2025）、FormL4——自然语言→Lean 的 alignment 评测开始成熟。**LeanCopilot 仍是最实用工具**，原生 Lean 内 `suggest_tactics` / `search_proof` / `select_premises`。LeanDojo-v2（NeurIPS 2025 workshop）作为基础设施稳定下来。\n\n## 跟 Phase 5 的潜在影响\n\n| 方向 | 影响 | 是否值得现在动 |\n|------|------|----------------|\n| HILBERT 风格 informal+formal 闭环 | 我们的 SAT/CP-SAT 反例 + Lean 形式证明可以套这个模板 | **可参考架构**，但 70x70 这种规模不需要递归分解 |\n| Leanstral / LeanCopilot | 把 mathlib 引理检索 + tactic 建议接进我们的 Phase 5 Lean 工程 | **高价值**，能把人类形式化时间砍掉 50-70% |\n| Goedel/Kimina/DeepSeek-Prover-V2 | 主要做竞赛题，跟\"最大空矩形精确性证明\"语义差距大 | 不直接用，**作为后备校验器** |\n| Gemini Deep Think / Claude 4.7 / GPT-5.5 | 做 informal proof sketch、数学命题翻译、tactic 建议 | **强烈建议主用 Claude 4.7 + Lean MCP** 做协作形式化 |\n| AlphaEvolve 系（CodeEvolve 等） | 算法发现，**不给形式保证** | 我们路线是 exact + proof，不需要 |\n| LLM-MILP（infeasibility-aware、LLM-LNS） | 让 LLM 当 LNS 邻域选择启发式 | 跟 Phase 3B 加速有关，**Phase 4 可考虑**，Phase 5 无关 |\n\n## 对 Phase 5 时间表的影响\n\n**结论：维持原节奏，但提前做两件低成本布局。**\n\n1. **现在就值得做的**（成本 < 1 周）：\n   - 把 LeanCopilot 装进 Phase 5 的 Lean 工程脚手架（提前装 = 进入形式化时直接用）\n   - 跟踪 Leanstral 在 FLT 项目的 PR，等它发 v2 / 稳定版\n   - Phase 5 spec 里加一个\"AI 协作形式化预算 budget\"字段，明确 AI 只做 tactic 建议 / 引理检索，不做证明源（跟 AI Safety Contract 一致）\n\n2. **不值得提前布局的**：\n   - Goedel-Prover / Kimina / DeepSeek-Prover：竞赛题分布，跟 70x70 网格 + ghost 矩形 + Benders 的语义 gap 太大，硬塞会浪费\n   - HILBERT 完整 agent 框架：我们问题规模相对窄，把它的 informal-formal 闭环理念学过来即可，不需要复刻整套 agent\n   - AlphaEvolve 系：明确不给形式保证，违反 Exactness Constitution\n\n3. **继续等的信号**：\n   - Leanstral 出 v2 / 在非 FLT 项目上的成功案例（说明它能泛化到组合优化形式证明）\n   - Lean mathlib 加 CP / SAT-style 推理库（目前 `Mathlib.Combinatorics` 在最大空矩形方向极薄）\n   - 有人公开发布\"形式化 CP-SAT 输出 → Lean 证明\"的工具链（**这是 Phase 5 最大的杠杆点**，可定期检索）\n\n**底线**：Phase 5（形式化）整体时间表不需要因这一波进展提前。AI 协作工具确实能把人类形式化工时砍下来，但 Phase 3B 还没跑完，先把 exact 证明跑通再说，AI 工具到时候只会更成熟。\n\n## Sources\n\n- [DeepSeek-Prover-V2 (arXiv 2504.21801)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.21801)\n- [Goedel-Prover-V2 (arXiv 2508.03613)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.03613)\n- [Goedel-Prover homepage](https://goedel-lm.github.io/)\n- [Hilbert: Recursively Building Formal Proofs (arXiv 2509.22819)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.22819)\n- [Apple ML Research — Hilbert](https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/hilbert)\n- [Kimina-Prover Preview (arXiv 2504.11354)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11354)\n- [Kimina-Prover-72B on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/AI-MO/Kimina-Prover-72B)\n- [Leanstral — Mistral AI](https://mistral.ai/news/leanstral)\n- [Mistral Leanstral coverage — The Register](https://www.theregister.com/2026/03/17/mistral_leanstral_ai_code_verification_tool/)\n- [Gemini Deep Think IMO Gold — DeepMind](https://deepmind.google/blog/advanced-version-of-gemini-with-deep-think-officially-achieves-gold-medal-standard-at-the-international-mathematical-olympiad/)\n- [Gemini Deep Think for scientific discovery — DeepMind](https://deepmind.google/blog/accelerating-mathematical-and-scientific-discovery-with-gemini-deep-think/)\n- [Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning — Nature](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y)\n- [STP: Self-play LLM Theorem Provers (arXiv 2502.00212)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.00212)\n- [Seed-Prover (arXiv 2507.23726)](https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2507.23726v1)\n- [CodeEvolve (arXiv 2510.14150)](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v1)\n- [Autoformalization Survey (arXiv 2505.23486)](https://arxiv.org/html/2505.23486v1)\n- [Lean Copilot — LeanDojo](https://leandojo.org/leancopilot.html)\n- [LeanCopilot GitHub](https://github.com/lean-dojo/LeanCopilot)\n- [LLMs for Combinatorial Optimization — ACM Computing Surveys](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3801961)\n- [What GenAI Taught Us About Global Optimization — ORMS Today](https://pubsonline.informs.org/do/10.1287/orms.2026.01.01/full/)\n- [Formal Reasoning Meets LLMs — CACM](https://cacm.acm.org/research/formal-reasoning-meets-llms-toward-ai-for-mathematics-and-verification/)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4624,"cache_read_input_tokens":35633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4624,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxsxH4GRcwmWBChV8bJ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"016982f4-ca5b-4165-a38f-3f3b4ef04847","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:04:11.941Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
